    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "act": "WHEN NOT TO",
      "narration_text": "So when should you use it? When the answer lives in documents you can point to, like a syllabus, a manual or last week's meeting notes, especially when those facts change. When shouldn't you? If the document is short, just paste it in. If you need reasoning or writing, not lookup, retrieval won't help much. And watch the search: if it grabs the wrong passage, you get a wrong answer that looks sourced.",
